WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.206
FedRAMP High has direct engineering implications.

2
00:00:03.206 --> 00:00:28.269
Strong identity and access control, privileged access management, least privilege, segmentation, encryption, secure configuration, vulnerability management, change control, audit logging, monitoring, incident response readiness, backup and recovery, resilience, secure development practices, infrastructure-as-code, and configuration baselines all become part of the operating picture.

3
00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:34.608
High-impact services should be secure, observable, recoverable, and evidence-producing by design.

4
00:00:34.608 --> 00:00:40.437
Secure means controls are built into architecture and workflows rather than patched on later.

5
00:00:40.437 --> 00:00:47.431
Observable means security-relevant events can be collected, protected, reviewed, and used for investigation.

6
00:00:47.431 --> 00:00:53.478
Recoverable means the service can respond to disruption in ways that match mission expectations.

7
00:00:53.478 --> 00:00:59.963
Evidence-producing means normal operations generate records that support assessment and monitoring.

8
00:00:59.963 --> 00:01:04.334
Engineering teams should reduce manual ambiguity wherever possible.

9
00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:10.382
Infrastructure-as-code can help enforce consistent environments and preserve change history.

10
00:01:10.382 --> 00:01:13.077
Configuration baselines can reduce drift.

11
00:01:13.077 --> 00:01:17.959
Centralized logging and monitoring can support detection and investigation.

12
00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:22.403
Automated vulnerability workflows can make remediation more visible.

13
00:01:22.403 --> 00:01:28.013
Access reviews, approval paths, and administrative logging can support accountability.

14
00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:32.385
These practices help the service sustain High expectations over time.

15
00:01:32.385 --> 00:01:34.716
High also requires maintainability.

16
00:01:34.716 --> 00:01:40.399
A control that depends on one specialist remembering an undocumented procedure is fragile.

17
00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:49.652
A control built into deployment pipelines, access systems, monitoring dashboards, ticketing workflows, and incident processes is more resilient.

18
00:01:49.652 --> 00:02:00.071
The engineering goal is not simply to produce evidence for an assessor; it is to operate a service whose security posture can be understood and maintained under pressure.
